/-!
# Local generation by `r` sections and finite type of `𝓗^a` on the five big sites

Descent, Lemma 05VG asserts, for each property of modules of Modules on Sites, Definitions
03DE, 03DL and 03ER, that a quasi-coherent `𝒪_S`-module `𝓗` has the property if and only if
`𝓗^a` has it as an `𝒪`-module on the site.  **This file proves two of those clauses at the big
site `(Sch/S)_τ`, at every `τ ∈ {Zariski, étale, smooth, syntomic, fppf}`**: the bounded
local-generation clause Definition 03DL (4) and the finite-type clause Definition 03DL (5),
each as an equivalence and each under the source's hypothesis that `𝓗` be quasi-coherent and
nothing else.

Both clauses are proved at the two small sites — `S_Zar` in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Descent/AssociatedModule/SmallZariskiLocalTypesComparison.lean`
and `S_étale` in `…/Descent/AssociatedModule/SmallEtaleLocalGenerationByRAgreement.lean` and
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Descent/AssociatedModule/SmallEtaleFinitenessAgreement.lean` — and
the unbounded clause 03DL (3) is proved at the big
site in `…/Descent/AssociatedModule/LocalGenerationBySectionsAgreement.lean`.  Neither small-site
route transfers: at `S_Zar` the comparison is an equivalence of ringed topoi, so Stacks 03DM
applies directly, and at `S_étale` the finite-type argument runs on the image-open factorization
of an étale morphism, which an arbitrary scheme over `S` does not have.

## The shape of the argument, and why it is the one of Definition 03DL (2)

Each clause splits into two implications of entirely different natures, exactly as for finite
local freeness.

**The `only if` half** is the covering argument at an open of `S`, and it needs no
quasi-coherence.  Stacks 03DN at the small Zariski site produces a Zariski covering of `S` on
whose members `𝓗` is generated by `r` sections (respectively by finitely many); the image of
that covering covers the final object of each of the five big sites,
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.coversTop_baseOpensToBig_ulift`; and on a member the localized
associated-module functor carries the generating family across without touching its index type,
because it preserves colimits and epimorphisms — being a left adjoint — and carries the unit
object to the unit object.  That transport is
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.generatingSectionsBaseAssociatedModuleOver`, built from
`Stacks.Sheaves.QcohTypeComparison.generatingSectionsMap` and the step Stacks 03DV leaves
implicit, `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.baseAssociatedModuleOverObjIso`.

**The `if` half** carries the mathematics and is proved at `τ = fppf` only, the four coarser
topologies being reached by monotonicity.  At `τ = fppf`: Stacks 03DN (respectively Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.IsFiniteType.exists_localGeneratorsData`) produces a family covering the final
object of `(Sch/S)_fppf` on whose members `𝓗^a` is generated by `r` (respectively finitely many)
sections; the members are arbitrary schemes over `S`, so
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.exists_coversTop_fpqc_refinement` refines the family to one whose
structure morphisms *are* an fpqc covering family of `S`, generation following the refinement
along the arrows of the site by `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatingSectionsOverMap`, which leaves
the index type alone.  On each member
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_pullback_of_over` turns the
verdict into generation of the pullback of `𝓗` by that many global sections, and the descent is
Stacks 082U for the bounded clause (`AlgebraicGeometry.isCardinalGenerated_of_pullback_fpqc`,
returned to the covering-family form of 03DL (4) by
`AlgebraicGeometry.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_of_isCardinalGenerated`) and Stacks 05AZ for
finite type (`AlgebraicGeometry.isFiniteType_of_pullback_fpqc`).

## The monotonicity, and why it is the left-adjoint route here

Both clauses are **weaker hypotheses at coarser `τ`**: a `τ`-covering family is an fppf covering
family, so the property for `(Sch/S)_τ` implies the property for `(Sch/S)_fppf`.  That
monotonicity is what confines the descent to one topology, and it is proved here for an
arbitrary pair of topologies `K ≤ J` on an arbitrary category:
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_of_comparisonPushforward` and
`…isFiniteType_of_comparisonPushforward`.

For finite *free*ness the analogous monotonicity is got from the **full faithfulness** of
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.comparisonPushforward`, which reflects a colimiting cofan.  That does not
serve here: what has to be reflected is an *epimorphism out of a free module*, and the free
module itself depends on the topology, being a sheafified coproduct.  So the route is the other
one — transport along the **left adjoint** `Stacks.SheafOfModules.comparisonPullback`, which
preserves colimits and epimorphisms, so
`Stacks.Sheaves.QcohTypeComparison.generatingSectionsMap` applies to it, and whose counit at a
module that is already a `J`-sheaf is invertible,
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.comparisonPullbackObjIso`.  The transported family is therefore a family
of generating sections of the module itself rather than of a sheafification, and its index type
is unchanged, so both the bound `r` and finiteness survive.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.comparisonPullbackUnitIso`: sheafification for the finer topology
  carries the structure sheaf read for the coarser topology back to the structure sheaf.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.generatingSectionsOfComparisonPushforward`: generating sections of the
  coarser reading of a module are generating sections of the module, with the same index type.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.generatingSectionsBaseAssociatedModuleOver`: generating sections
  of `𝓗|_V` over an open `V` of `S` give generating sections of `(𝓗^a)|_{(Sch/V)_τ}`, with the
  same index type.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_of_comparisonPushforward` and
  `…isFiniteType_of_comparisonPushforward`: local generation by `r` sections and finite type for
  a coarser topology imply the same for a finer one, for an arbitrary pair of topologies on one
  category and with no further hypothesis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_pullback_of_over`: generation
  of `(𝓗^a)|_{(Sch/S)_fppf/T}` by `r` sections is generation of `f^*𝓗` by `r` global sections,
  for `f` the structure morphism of an object `T`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isLocallyGeneratedByOnSite_baseAssociatedModule_iff`:
  **Descent, Lemma 05VG for Modules on Sites, Definition 03DL (4), at the big site `(Sch/S)_τ`
  for every `τ`, as an equivalence.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isFiniteType_baseAssociatedModule_iff`:
  **Descent, Lemma 05VG for Modules on Sites, Definition 03DL (5), at the big site `(Sch/S)_τ`
  for every `τ`, as an equivalence.**

## Implementation notes

The `τ`-analogue of Stacks 03DV functorial in an *arbitrary object* of the big site,
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.associatedModuleObjRestrictNatIso`, exists at `τ = fppf` and at no
other `τ`; it is used only inside
`AlgebraicGeometry.BigFppfOver.isGeneratedByGlobalSectionsOfCard_pullback_of_over`, which the
monotonicity confines to that one topology.  At an *open* of `S` the analogue is available at
every `τ`, which is what the `only if` halves use.

The index universe of the covering family of Stacks 03DN at the big site is `u + 1`, the universe
of the site's objects, and so is the index universe of the fpqc covering family of `S` produced
from it; both `AlgebraicGeometry.isCardinalGenerated_of_pullback_fpqc` and
`AlgebraicGeometry.isFiniteType_of_pullback_fpqc` are stated at an arbitrary index universe and
so admit it.

The two readings of one module over a member of the covering — restrict to the slice then read
for the coarser topology, or read for the coarser topology then restrict — are the same sheaf of
modules, and that holds by `rfl`: restriction to a slice site changes only the underlying
presheaf's index category, and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.comparisonPushforward` changes neither the
presheaf nor the morphisms.  This is what lets the slice-wise steps of the monotonicity be
written with `Stacks.SheafOfModules.over_le_over_of_le`.

